-- title:
--   Closure of a generic-fibre divisor avoids special-fibre generic points
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$ and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ be the intermediate field obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image ([`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81)) of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the $j$-invariant; write $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ for [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252). Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and let $C_1, C_2$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$, geometrically integral $k$-schemes, equipped with closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ into $X \times_A \operatorname{Spec} k$, whose images together cover $X \times_A \operatorname{Spec} k$, with $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$ reduced and of cardinality $n > 0$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain and $\rho_O : A \to O$ a ring map with $\rho_O(\mathfrak m_A)$ generating $\mathfrak m_O$, let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ be a surjective ring map with $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O$ the $A$-algebra structure of $k$, and let $bc : X \times_A \operatorname{Spec} k \to X \times_A \operatorname{Spec} O$ be a morphism compatible with the projections to $X$ and covering $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$. Assume the ideal-sheaf kernels of $i_1 \!\gg\! bc$ and $i_2 \!\gg\! bc$ are invertible, in the sense that each point has an affine open $U$ and $f \in \Gamma(U)$ with the point in the basic open of $f$ and the ideal on the affine basic open of $f$ generated by a single non-zero-divisor, and that the product of these two kernels is the kernel of $bc$. Let $T'$ be the fraction field of $O$, assume $X \times_A \operatorname{Spec} T' \to \operatorname{Spec} T'$ smooth of relative dimension $1$, and let $E$ (over $\operatorname{Spec} T'$) and $\bar E$ (over $\operatorname{Spec} O$) be relative effective Cartier divisors of degree $r$ on $X$, i.e. ideal sheaves whose closed subschemes are finite, flat and locally of finite presentation over the base with fibre rank $r$ everywhere, such that the ideal of $\bar E$ is the kernel of the closed subscheme of $E$ mapped into $X \times_A \operatorname{Spec} O$, and such that for every irreducible $\varpi \in O$, every affine open $U$ and every $s \in \Gamma(U)$, if the product of $s$ with the image of $\varpi$ under the structure map lies in the ideal of $\bar E$ on $U$ then so does $s$. Then: every point $\xi$ of $X \times_A \operatorname{Spec} k$ that is maximal for specialisation (the only $y$ specialising to $\xi$ is $\xi$) has $bc(\xi)$ outside the support of the ideal of $\bar E$; and there exist points $c \in C_1$ and $c \in C_2$ whose images under $i_1 \!\gg\! bc$, respectively $i_2 \!\gg\! bc$, lie outside that support.
--
--   This is the "no vertical component" property of the schematic closure over a discrete valuation ring, in the concrete setting of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$: the closure of a relative divisor on the generic fibre, being finite over the base, meets the special fibre in finitely many points and so misses the generic points of its components, and in particular misses points on each of the two components $C_1$, $C_2$. It feeds the statements that the ideal of the closure is locally generated by a single non-zero-divisor and that the closure is a relative effective Cartier divisor with invertible ideal after pullback.
